WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.520
Quantum threats matter because security planning has to begin before a crisis is visible.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.165
The practical concern is not that every current system is already broken.

00:00:10.165 --> 00:00:15.972
The concern is that large cryptographically relevant quantum computers could weaken widely used public-key cryptography,

00:00:15.972 --> 00:00:21.392
and the systems that depend on that cryptography often take years to discover, change,

00:00:21.392 --> 00:00:22.940
test, approve, and deploy.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.424
Security practitioners need to distinguish present-day risk, future capability,

00:00:26.424 --> 00:00:27.973
and migration lead time.

00:00:27.973 --> 00:00:32.231
Present-day risk includes data being collected now, systems being designed now,

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:34.166
and products being purchased now.

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:38.812
Future capability refers to the possibility that quantum computers eventually become strong

00:00:38.812 --> 00:00:41.135
enough to attack certain public-key schemes.

00:00:41.135 --> 00:00:47.328
Migration lead time is the gap between deciding to change and actually changing complex systems safely.

00:00:47.328 --> 00:00:51.587
Public-key cryptography is the central concern because it supports key exchange,

00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:55.458
digital signatures, certificates, identity, software trust, and many secure protocols.

00:00:55.458 --> 00:01:00.878
Symmetric cryptography and hashing are affected differently, and the response is not the same.

00:01:00.878 --> 00:01:04.749
The migration problem is therefore not simply replace encryption everywhere.

00:01:04.749 --> 00:01:08.620
It is identify where specific public-key functions create future exposure.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:13.265
Planning matters most for systems with long lifetimes, long data sensitivity periods,

00:01:13.265 --> 00:01:14.427
and complex dependencies.

00:01:14.427 --> 00:01:19.846
A web service that can be updated monthly is different from a medical device,

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.556
satellite, vehicle, industrial controller, or long-lived archive.

00:01:22.556 --> 00:01:25.653
The goal of quantum readiness is not fear.

00:01:25.653 --> 00:01:30.686
It is disciplined preparation while there is still time to inventory, prioritize, test,

00:01:30.686 --> 00:01:31.460
and coordinate.
